Chapter: IdentityBasic

 The identity words start zero, an out-of-range read is -1, and a set
 is visible to a later whoami. identity-set carries the Identity
 effect, so this program declares it and the boot grant derived from
 its own manifest supplies the capability bit the kernel checks.
 Reading a word with identity-whoami is Identity as well as writing
 one, so the helpers that read name the effect too. Each effectful set
 is threaded through a step helper in argument position, the
 sanctioned position for an effectful call outside an act-bind.

Section: Body
  initial-ok : Integer -> [Identity] Boolean
  initial-ok (x) =
    if identity-whoami 0 /= 0 then False
    else if identity-whoami 1 /= 0 then False
    else if identity-whoami 2 /= 0 then False
    else if identity-whoami 3 /= 0 then False
    else identity-whoami 4 == (0 - 1)

  after-set1 : Integer -> [Identity] Text
  after-set1 (s1) =
    if s1 /= 0 then "FAIL: set1 returned error"
    else if identity-whoami 0 /= 42 then "FAIL: word 0 not set"
    else if identity-whoami 1 /= 99 then "FAIL: word 1 not set"
    else "PASS"

  after-set0 : Integer -> [Identity] Text
  after-set0 (s0) =
    if s0 /= 0 then "FAIL: set0 returned error"
    else after-set1 (identity-set 1 99)

  run-basic : Integer -> [Identity] Text
  run-basic (x) =
    if initial-ok 0 == False then "FAIL: initial words not zero"
    else after-set0 (identity-set 0 42)

  opening : [Console, Identity] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (run-basic 0)
  end
